<title>USA: American Pad Q3 oper shr $0.24 vs $0.16.</title>
<headline>American Pad Q3 oper shr $0.24 vs $0.16.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Pad &amp; Paper Co.</p>
<p>			     (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>					Three Months Ended September 30</p>
<p>				     1996	1995     1996     1995</p>
<p>					 Actual	    Pro forma</p>
<p> Net sales		   $173,606   $53,787 $173,606 $155,832</p>
<p> Gross profit		  36,037    10,258   36,037   30,995</p>
<p> Operating income	    21,725     7,071   22,976   19,017</p>
<p>Income before</p>
<p> extraordinary item	 6,925     4,850    8,867  7,381 (a)</p>
<p> Net income/ (loss)	(11,770)     4,850  (9,828)    7,381</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>  shares outstanding	 29,351    29,607   29,607   29,607</p>
<p>Earning per share before</p>
<p>  extraordinary item	   0.24	0.16     0.30     0.25</p>
<p>(a) The pro forma net income for the three months ended Sept. 30, 1995 has been adjusted to reflect an annualized effective tax rate of 36.1 percent, the company's pro forma effective tax rate for all of 1995.  The previously published pro forma net income information for 1995 reflected an unusually low tax rate in the third quarter of 1995 due to the use of a loss carryforward.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
